From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: disable unstable CPU retention states

The SM8750 CPU retention states enter s2idle but fail to return from
RTC- or power-button-triggered wake on the AYN Odin 3. The same device
wakes reliably when these states are disabled and the CPUs use WFI.

The UFS controller has been observed to complete system suspend with the
link in UIC_LINK_OFF_STATE before the hang, so avoid changing UFS power
management for this platform issue. Keep the idle-state definitions
available for future firmware validation, but do not expose them to the
generic CPU idle-state parser.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -180,4 +180,5 @@
 				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				status = "disabled";
 				idle-state-name = "ret";
 				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00000004>;
 				entry-latency-us = <93>;
@@ -189,4 +190,5 @@
 				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				status = "disabled";
 				idle-state-name = "ret";
 				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00000004>;
 				entry-latency-us = <172>;
